Article 4 An arbitration agreement includes an arbitration clause stipulated in a contract and any other written agreement concluded before or after a dispute arises providing for arbitration.
An arbitration agreement shall contain the following:
(1) an expression of intention to request arbitration;
(2) matters for arbitration;
(3) an expression of intention to select this Arbitration Commission.

Article 7 A party applying for arbitration shall meet the following conditions:
(1) there is an arbitration agreement;
(2) there are specific arbitration claims, facts, and reasons;
(3) the case falls within the jurisdiction of this Arbitration Commission.

Article 9 The application for arbitration shall state the following:
(1) the name, sex, age, occupation, employer and domicile of the applicant and the respondent, or the name and domicile of the legal person or any other organization and the name and position of the legal representative or the principal person in charge;
(2) the arbitration claim and the facts and reasons on which it is based;
(3) the evidence and the source of evidence, and the name and domicile of any witness.

Article 19 An arbitrator shall withdraw in any of the following circumstances, and a party shall also have the right to apply for withdrawal:
(1) the arbitrator is a close relative of a party or of an agent of a party in the case;
(2) the arbitrator has an interest in the case;
(3) the arbitrator has any other relationship with a party or an agent of a party that may affect the impartiality of the arbitration;
(4) the arbitrator has had a private meeting with a party or an agent or has accepted entertainment or gifts from a party or an agent.

Article 4 An arbitration agreement includes an arbitration clause stipulated in a contract and any other written agreement concluded before or after the occurrence of a dispute requesting arbitration.
An arbitration agreement shall contain the following:
(1) An expression of intention to request arbitration;
(2) Matters subject to arbitration;
(3) An expression of intention to select this Arbitration Commission.

Article 7 A party applying for arbitration shall meet the following conditions:
(1) There is an arbitration agreement;
(2) There is a specific arbitration claim and relevant facts and reasons;
(3) The matter falls within the jurisdiction of this Arbitration Commission.

Article 9 The application for arbitration shall specify the following:
(1) The name, gender, age, occupation, work unit and domicile of the applicant and the respondent, and the name and domicile of the legal person or other organization and the name and position of its legal representative or principal responsible person;
(2) The arbitration claim and the facts and reasons on which it is based;
(3) The evidence and the source of evidence, and the name and domicile of the witness.

Article 19 An arbitrator must withdraw from the case under any of the following circumstances, and the parties also have the right to apply for his or her withdrawal:
(1) The arbitrator is a close relative of a party or of an agent of a party in the case;
(2) The arbitrator has an interest in the case;
(3) The arbitrator has other relations with a party or an agent of a party in the case that may affect the impartiality of the arbitration;
(4) The arbitrator has privately met with a party or an agent or accepted a party's or agent's hospitality.

Article 46 A party may, within six months from receipt of the arbitral award, apply to the Intermediate People's Court in the place where this arbitration commission is located for setting aside the award, if it provides evidence that:
(1) there is no arbitration agreement;
(2) the matters decided in the award fall outside the scope of the arbitration agreement or the arbitration commission has no power to arbitrate;
(3) the formation of the arbitral tribunal or the arbitration procedure was not in accordance with statutory procedures;
(4) the evidence on which the award is based was forged;
(5) the other party has concealed evidence sufficient to affect the impartiality of the award; or
(6) an arbitrator, in arbitrating the case, committed acts of soliciting or accepting bribes, engaging in malpractice for personal gain, or perverting the law in making the award.
